# GTT — Cursor integration

This repository is governed by **GTT (Governance Throw Think)**. The full
agent contract is `AGENTS.md` at the repository root — Cursor loads it on its
own; read it before proposing or making any change. This rule adds only what
Cursor needs beyond that. It is an integration surface, never a second copy of
the methodology and never a source of authority.

## Read first

- `AGENTS.md` — the portable GTT contract.
- `gtt-domain/context/constraints.md` — hard limits that apply to every change.
- `.gtt/docs/index.md` — the map of every file in this kit.

## What Cursor must not do

`gtt-domain/context/`, `gtt-domain/adr/`, `gtt-domain/change-request.md`,
`SOURCE-BRIEF.*` and `AGENTS.md` are governed paths owned by the Solution
Designer. `.cursor/hooks.json` denies a write or a shell command that reaches
them, but that hook has not been verified inside Cursor and it is not what
makes the rule binding: treat this instruction as binding on its own. To propose a change,
write a draft under `gtt-domain/proposals/` and follow the change process in
`AGENTS.md`; never edit the governed paths directly, and never work around this
by renaming, duplicating or editing them through another path — including
through the terminal.

The same applies to any file, class or method carrying a `@GTTGuard` marker
(listed in `.gtt/protection/registry.yaml`) — see `AGENTS.md` → *Protected
artifacts (GTTGuard)*. `.gtt/scripts/gtt-check-protection.sh` in CI is the
actual enforcement.

Never run a promotion script (`gtt-domain/proposals/apply-*.sh`). Prepare it;
the human runs it.

## Speaking for GTT

When a message is GTT's — a question the method needs answered, a confirmation
or choice, the Initial Design Questionnaire, the Design Assessment, a
proposal, a finding, a request for authorization, a report — open it with
`@gtt · <what this is>` (`@gtt · Method Plan`, `@gtt · Report`). Ordinary work
carries no marker, and the marker is never a decision or an approval.

## Procedures

GTT's procedures (bootstrap, propose a change, design an Epic, record an ADR,
audit) are described in `AGENTS.md` — follow those steps directly. After any
operation run `bash .gtt/scripts/gtt-maintain.sh`. When a step calls for a
judgment `AGENTS.md` does not resolve, ask the Solution Designer rather than
improvising.
